examples.question_text:
Use Pythagoras’ theorem to find $h$, then calculate the exact area of this right-angled triangle.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(3,0)--(0,4)--cycle;
\draw (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\path (1.5,0) node[below] {$5\text{ m}$} (0,2) node[left] {$h$} (1.5,2) node[above right] {$8\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the perpendicular height $h$, then calculate the area of this isosceles triangle to $2$ decimal places.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(4,0)--(2,4)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (2,0)--(2,4);
\draw (2,0.25)--(2.25,0.25)--(2.25,0);
\path (2,0) node[below] {$10\text{ cm}$} (1,2) node[above left] {$12\text{ cm}$} (3,2) node[above right] {$12\text{ cm}$} (2,2) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the height $h$ of this trapezium, then calculate its area.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(5,0)--(5,3)--(2,3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (2,3)--(2,0);
\draw (2,0.25)--(2.25,0.25)--(2.25,0);
\draw (4.75,0)--(4.75,0.25)--(5,0.25);
\draw (4.75,3)--(4.75,2.75)--(5,2.75);
\path (2.5,0) node[below] {$23\text{ cm}$} (3.5,3) node[above] {$14\text{ cm}$} (1,1.5) node[above left] {$15\text{ cm}$} (5,1.5) node[right] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the height $h$ of this isosceles trapezium, then calculate its area to $1$ decimal place.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(5,0)--(4,3)--(1,3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (1,3)--(1,0) (4,3)--(4,0);
\draw (1,0.25)--(1.25,0.25)--(1.25,0);
\draw (4,0.25)--(4.25,0.25)--(4.25,0);
\path (2.5,0) node[below] {$26\text{ cm}$} (2.5,3) node[above] {$14\text{ cm}$} (0.5,1.5) node[above left] {$9\text{ cm}$} (4.5,1.5) node[above right] {$9\text{ cm}$} (1,1.5) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The horizontal diagonal of this kite is bisected by the vertical diagonal. Find $a$ and $b$, then calculate the area of the kite.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,2)--(2,0)--(0,-3)--(-2,0)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (-2,0)--(2,0) (0,2)--(0,-3);
\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);
\path (1,0) node[below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$6\text{ cm}$} (0,1) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$a$} (0,-1.5) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$b$} (1,1) node[above right] {$10\text{ cm}$} (-1,1) node[above left] {$10\text{ cm}$} (1,-1.5) node[below right] {$15\text{ cm}$} (-1,-1.5) node[below left] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A rhombus has side length $17\text{ cm}$ and one diagonal of length $16\text{ cm}$. Find its area.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.6,0)--(0,3)--(1.6,0)--(0,-3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (-1.6,0)--(1.6,0) (0,3)--(0,-3);
\draw (0,0.25)--(0.25,0.25)--(0.25,0);
\path (0.8,1.5) node[above right] {$17\text{ cm}$} (0,1.5) node[left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$m$};
\draw[<->] (-1.6,-3.5)--(1.6,-3.5);
\path (0,-3.5) node[below] {$16\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A square has a diagonal of length $16\text{ cm}$. Use Pythagoras’ theorem to find its area.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3.5,3.5);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(3.5,3.5);
\draw (3.25,0)--(3.25,0.25)--(3.5,0.25);
\path (1.75,0) node[below] {$x$} (3.5,1.75) node[right] {$x$} (1.5,1.5) node[above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$16\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the exact area of this equilateral triangle, giving your answer in simplified form.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(4,0)--(2,3.464)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (2,3.464)--(2,0);
\draw (2,0.25)--(2.25,0.25)--(2.25,0);
\path (2,0) node[below] {$12\text{ cm}$} (1,1.732) node[above left] {$12\text{ cm}$} (3,1.732) node[above right] {$12\text{ cm}$} (2,1.6) node[right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
